  "problem": "A data set has a mean $\\overset{\u00af}{x}=-100$ and an unknown standard deviation. An observation of the data set has the value $x=-83$ and $z$-score $z=1.7.$ Find the standard deviation of the data set.",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-83,$ $\\overset{\u00af}{x}=-100,$ and $z=1.7$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{\u2015}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ -83 & =-100+1.7\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 17 & =1.7\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
